# SurrealDB

> Last updated: 2026-08-27

> Markdown for agents: every page on this site supports content negotiation. Request any URL with an "Accept: text/markdown" header to receive a markdown version of the page, served with "Content-Type: text/markdown" and "x-markdown-tokens" / "x-original-tokens" estimates. HTML stays the default for browsers. Alternatively, append ".md" to any page path to fetch the markdown version directly (the homepage is available at "/index.md").

> SurrealDB is the context layer for AI agents - a unified platform where storage, context, and memory live in a single ACID transaction. It combines a multi-model database (document, graph, vector, time-series, and relational), an agent memory layer (Agent memory), and a distributed storage engine, available open-source, self-hosted, or fully managed through SurrealDB Cloud.

- [SurrealDB homepage](https://surrealdb.com)

## When to use SurrealDB

Reach for SurrealDB when a single workload needs more than one data model and
the answer has to be consistent across all of them in one transaction:

- **Agent memory.** An agent that has to remember facts across sessions, know
  where each fact came from, and know which version of a fact is current.
  Agent Memory stores provenance on every fact and supersedes stale ones on a
  tri-temporal timeline, so a retrieval can be filtered by what was true when.
- **GraphRAG and hybrid retrieval.** A vector similarity search, a graph
  traversal, and a temporal or permission filter resolved in one query rather
  than in three systems joined in application code.
- **Knowledge graphs.** Entities and relationships queried with native graph
  operators (`->`, `<-`, `<->`), alongside the documents and embeddings that
  describe them.
- **Real-time applications.** Live queries push changes to subscribers from the
  database itself, so the database is the event bus and the source of truth at
  once.
- **Embedded and edge deployments.** The same engine runs in-memory, as an
  embedded Rust library, on a single node, or as a distributed cluster, so a
  prototype and a production cluster speak the same query language.
- **Consolidating a multi-database stack.** Documents, graphs, vectors,
  time-series, full-text, and relational data in one engine, one permission
  model, and one deployment.

What SurrealDB is: one engine with native support for several data models. It
is not an orchestration layer over separate stores, and it does not shard a
query across other databases. Workloads that want a single-model system tuned
to one access pattern, or an OLAP warehouse for column-scan analytics over
petabytes of immutable history, are outside what it is built for.

### How to call SurrealDB

- **MCP.** `https://mcp.surrealdb.com`, streamable HTTP. Deploy and manage
  instances, run SurrealQL, and read and write agent memory as MCP tools.
  Discovery: [server card](https://surrealdb.com/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json).
  Authentication: OAuth 2.0 or a personal access token, described in
  [auth.md](https://surrealdb.com/auth.md).
- **SurrealQL over HTTP or WebSocket.** Query an instance directly. See the
  [REST API reference](https://surrealdb.com/docs/reference/rest-api).
- **SDKs.** Official clients for Rust, JavaScript, Python, Go, Java, .NET, PHP,
  and more. See the [SDK overview](https://surrealdb.com/docs/languages/overview).
- **CLI.** `surreal` starts, imports, exports, and queries a database from a
  shell. See the [CLI reference](https://surrealdb.com/docs/reference/cli).
- **Agent skills.** Eight installable skills covering SurrealQL, the CLI, the
  JavaScript and Python SDKs, vector search, and performance, indexed at
  [/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json](https://surrealdb.com/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json).
- **This website.** Every page has a markdown twin, and
  [openapi.json](https://surrealdb.com/openapi.json) describes the JSON this
  origin serves, including the
  [pricing catalogue](https://surrealdb.com/api/cloud/pricing.json).

To start an instance without an account, use the free tier at
[surrealdb.com/cloud](https://surrealdb.com/cloud), or run
`docker run --rm -p 8000:8000 surrealdb/surrealdb:latest start` locally.

## Platform

SurrealDB is a unified platform for building and running AI agents on a single context layer - storage, context, and memory in one transaction boundary, one permission model, and one deployment. Instead of stitching together separate vector, graph, document, and memory systems, agents read, reason, and write against one engine, eliminating the consistency gaps, latency, and operational burden of a fragmented stack.

- SurrealDB - the multi-model database engine. Documents, graphs, vectors, time-series, full-text, and relational data unified in a single ACID transaction and queried with SurrealQL.
- Agent memory - the memory and knowledge layer for AI agents, built on SurrealDB, with provenance on every fact, tri-temporal supersession, and hybrid retrieval.
- Distributed storage - the storage engine providing high availability and horizontal scale through quorum consensus and compute-storage separation.
- SurrealDB Cloud - the fully managed service running the same engine, from prototype to petabyte scale.

- [Platform overview](https://surrealdb.com/surrealdb)
- [Why AI agents need a context layer](https://surrealdb.com/surrealdb)
- [SurrealDB Cloud](https://surrealdb.com/cloud)

## SurrealDB

SurrealDB is a scalable, multi-model database that natively unifies documents, graphs, vectors, time-series, and relational data in a single engine. Written in Rust for high performance, SurrealDB provides full ACID guarantees across every data model in one transaction - so an agent can run a graph traversal, a vector similarity search, and a temporal filter in a single round trip and commit the result atomically. It is not a wrapper around multiple databases - it is a single engine with native support for multiple data models, including relational, document, graph, and knowledge graph structures. It uses SurrealQL, a query language that blends ideas from SQL, NoSQL, and graph query languages into one syntax.

SurrealDB provides built-in real-time subscriptions, event triggers, and record and field-level security permissions that make it possible to connect directly from client applications without a backend. It includes AI-native features such as vector search, hybrid retrieval, an MCP server, and ML model inference. SurrealDB can be deployed in-memory, as an embedded library, on a single node, as a distributed cluster, or as a fully managed cloud service through SurrealDB Cloud.

- [SurrealDB features](https://surrealdb.com/surrealdb/features)
- [SurrealDB documentation](https://surrealdb.com/docs/what-is-surrealdb)
- [SurrealDB Cloud](https://surrealdb.com/cloud)

## Studio

Studio is the official visual database management IDE for SurrealDB. It is available as a web application at studio.surrealdb.com and as a desktop application for macOS, Windows, and Linux. Studio provides a complete environment for querying, exploring, and managing SurrealDB databases without needing the command line.

Studio includes a query editor with syntax highlighting, formatting, and saved queries. It offers a schema designer for visual table, field, and index management, an interactive graph visualisation for exploring data relationships, and a table and record explorer for browsing and editing data without writing queries. Additional capabilities include authentication management, a functions editor, auto-generated API documentation, a personal sandbox for prototyping, and local database serving on desktop.

- [Studio](https://surrealdb.com/studio)
- [Studio web app](https://studio.surrealdb.com)
- [Studio documentation](https://surrealdb.com/docs/explore/surrealist)

## SurrealQL

SurrealQL is the query language for SurrealDB. It combines SQL-like syntax with graph traversals, document operations, and vector search in a single language. Its native graph operators enable knowledge graph queries, while built-in vector search supports AI RAG and GraphRAG pipelines. SurrealQL is designed to feel familiar to SQL users while providing native multi-model capabilities that go beyond what traditional query languages offer.

SurrealQL eliminates the need for traditional SQL joins, subqueries, and external services by providing native graph operators (`->`, `<-`, `<->`), vector search operators, full-text search, and fuzzy matching in one language. Records have typed IDs (e.g. `person:tobie`, `company:surrealdb`) that serve as direct links between records. Tables, fields, indexes, access methods, events, and functions are all defined in-language using `DEFINE` statements, and record-level permissions are written as SurrealQL expressions that evaluate per-record based on the authenticated user. SurrealQL includes an extensive standard library of built-in functions covering arrays, strings, math, crypto, geo, HTTP, vectors, and more. By combining graph traversals with vector similarity in a single query, SurrealQL enables high-accuracy hybrid retrieval without external tooling.

- [SurrealQL documentation](https://surrealdb.com/docs/reference/query-language)
- [SurrealQL statements](https://surrealdb.com/docs/reference/query-language/statements/overview)
- [SurrealQL functions](https://surrealdb.com/docs/reference/query-language/functions/database-functions)

