## Products

- [SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/surrealdb/features): The open-source multi-model database engine
- [SurrealDB Cloud](https://surrealdb.com/cloud): Fully managed cloud database service with automatic backups, monitoring, and scaling
- [Studio](https://surrealdb.com/studio): Visual database management IDE available as a web and desktop application
- [Agent memory](https://surrealdb.com/agent-memory): Memory and knowledge layer for AI agents, built on SurrealDB. Provenance on every fact, tri-temporal supersession, scope-bound multi-tenancy, ACID across graph, vector, document and structured records, hybrid retrieval (vector + BM25 + graph + keyword + geographic), and an MCP server built into the binary. Agent memory is waitlist-gated pre-launch - join the waitlist for early access; at launch a free Sandbox plan includes 3M tokens as a one-off grant, and the paid plans are $30 a month (Agent memory Lite, 1M tokens per month), $300 (Agent memory Standard, 10M) and $1,100 (Agent memory Plus, 40M); Enterprise is priced via sales. The managed service runs on SurrealDB Cloud, covered by SOC 2 Type 2, ISO 27001, GDPR, CCPA, and Cyber Essentials Plus.
- [Agent memory pricing](https://surrealdb.com/agent-memory#pricing): Agent memory plans and the full feature matrix - Sandbox free (3M tokens, one-off), Agent memory Lite $30/mo, Agent memory Standard $300/mo, Agent memory Plus $1,100/mo, Enterprise custom
- [Agent memory design partners](https://surrealdb.com/agent-memory/get-started): The Agent memory design-partner application
- [Agent memory deep dive](https://surrealdb.com/agent-memory/deep-dive): The full technical treatment of the Agent memory engine - memory categories, document pipeline, hybrid retrieval, tiered queries, audit and time
- [Extensions](https://surrealdb.com/surrealdb/extensions): WebAssembly-based extension framework for running custom logic inside SurrealDB
- [SurrealDB University](https://surrealdb.com/learn): Free interactive learning platform with courses, labs, and certifications
- [Enterprise](https://surrealdb.com/enterprise): Enterprise-grade deployment with high-performance clustering, data accuracy guarantees, knowledge graph support, dedicated support, and compliance certifications
- [Open source](https://surrealdb.com/opensource): Open-source programme and licensing

## AI and agent tools

SurrealDB provides integrated tools for AI and agentic workflows, combining graph and vector retrieval to power AI RAG and GraphRAG pipelines. Its unified data model supports persistent agent memory, enabling AI agents to store, traverse, and retrieve context with high accuracy - all without external middleware.

- [Connect your agent](https://surrealdb.com/docs/build/ai-agents): MCP, Agent Skills, and AI framework integrations
- [MCP Server](https://surrealdb.com/mcp): Hosted MCP server at https://mcp.surrealdb.com for connecting AI tools to SurrealDB Cloud
- [Platform API](https://api.surrealdb.com/docs): Public HTTP control-plane API for managing SurrealDB Cloud and connecting to instances and contexts. OpenAPI 3.0 description at https://api.surrealdb.com/openapi/public.yaml. Bearer JWT auth; the authorization server is https://auth.surrealdb.com.
- [Docs over SSH](https://surrealdb.sh): The full SurrealDB documentation as a read-only filesystem an agent can browse from a terminal. Run "ssh surrealdb.sh" and explore the docs at /surrealdb/docs with grep, cat, find and awk. No API key, no auth, isolated sandbox. Run "ssh surrealdb.sh setup | claude" to configure Claude Code with the doc context, or "ssh surrealdb.sh agents >> AGENTS.md" to append doc-checking rules to CLAUDE.md, GEMINI.md, AGENTS.md or any other agent rules file.
- [auth.md](https://surrealdb.com/auth.md): How an agent gets a credential for the surfaces that need one, in the auth.md format - the MCP server (resource https://mcp.surrealdb.com) and the platform API (audience https://api.surrealdb.com/api), the two supported methods (interactive OAuth 2.1 with dynamic client registration, or a scoped personal access token from https://account.surrealdb.com/tokens), scopes, bearer usage, and revocation. This site itself needs no credential. Discovery on this origin (HTTP 200 JSON): [Protected Resource Metadata](https://surrealdb.com/.well-known/oauth-protected-resource) and [Authorization Server metadata](https://surrealdb.com/.well-known/oauth-authorization-server). `agent_auth.register_uri` is the MCP dynamic-client-registration endpoint. Agent-attested registration (ID-JAG identity assertions, service_auth, anonymous claim ceremony) is not implemented.
- [Agent Skills](https://github.com/surrealdb/agent-skills): Official SurrealDB agent skills for use in agentic workflows, compatible with Claude Code, GitHub Copilot, Cursor, Cline, and other AI agents. Includes skills for SurrealQL, vector search, and the Python SDK.
- [Agent memory](https://surrealdb.com/agent-memory): Memory and knowledge layer for AI agents, built on SurrealDB. Provenance on every fact, tri-temporal supersession, engine-enforced multi-tenancy, ACID across graph, vector, document and structured records. Hybrid retrieval over vector, lexical, graph, keyword, and geographic signals. MCP server built into the binary; works with Cursor, Claude Desktop, Windsurf, VS Code, and Claude Code. Waitlist-gated pre-launch - join the waitlist for early access; at launch a free Sandbox plan and paid plans from $30 a month; Enterprise via sales.

## Getting started

SurrealDB can be installed on macOS, Linux, and Windows as a single binary, or run via Docker. Once installed, a local database can be started with a single command. Each SDK provides a quick start guide for connecting to SurrealDB from your preferred language, and SurrealDB Cloud offers a managed option that requires no local setup.

- [Install SurrealDB](https://surrealdb.com/surrealdb/install): Installation instructions for all platforms
